#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:1
msgid "Determinism and observable order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:3
msgid ""
"*Implemented.* What the engine guarantees about order, what it does not, "
"and why the guarantee was deliberately weakened in exactly one place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:6
msgid "Ordered maps where order is observable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:8
msgid ""
"Promise maps, schedule steps and pipe order all use **insertion or key "
"order**, never hash order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:10
msgid ""
"**Rejected: hash maps**, which are faster and were what the Python "
"original used for some of these."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:12
msgid ""
"The cost of hash order is not correctness but **reproducibility**, in two"
" specific ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:14
msgid "the order pages are processed in determines the order of the output rows;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:15
msgid ""
"the order ids are visited in determines **which cycle** a promise failure"
" reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:17
msgid ""
"A test that passes four times out of five is worse than a slower map. An "
"error message that names a different cycle on each run cannot be "
"asserted, so it stops being tested, so it stops being maintained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:21
msgid "What determinism guarantees"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "Guaranteed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "output tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "**byte-identical** regardless of the parallelism settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "row order within a table"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "deterministic for the same inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "the cycle a promise error reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "the same cycle every time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "`.log.csv` rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md
msgid "sorted, and identical between one worker and many"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:29
msgid ""
"The first is the strong one, and it is tested rather than asserted: the "
"same run at one worker and at N produces the same files, checked in the "
"integration suite and by checksum against the formats repository's "
"reference outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:33
msgid "The one place determinism was relaxed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:34
msgid ""
"Byte-for-byte determinism was the original requirement for the parallel "
"work. It was relaxed, on purpose, to **semantic equivalence**: the "
"parallel output must contain the same data, not necessarily in the same "
"order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:38
msgid ""
"The relaxation was needed because a strict reading would have excluded "
"the cheapest collection strategies. What happened next is worth "
"recording:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:41
msgid ""
"**The licence to diverge was taken and then not used.** Results from jobs"
" are collected in **indexed slots**, which costs nothing, so the "
"aggregated tables stay byte-identical anyway. The margin was spent only "
"on **merging log files**, where the children's lines are poured into the "
"parent's in job order rather than in the instant they happened."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:46
msgid ""
"That is the ideal outcome for that kind of permission, and it is why "
"reference outputs remain comparable by checksum even though the "
"constraint that protected them was formally dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:49
msgid "What determinism does not guarantee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:50
msgid ""
"**The interleaving of log lines across concurrent jobs.** Two jobs "
"running at once produce lines in whatever order they happen; the merge "
"restores job order at the end, not the original instants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:53
msgid "**Wall-clock timing in the logs**, obviously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/determinism.md:55
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**That a page is processed on any particular thread or process**, which "
"nothing downstream may depend on — that is the whole content of "
"{doc}`pages`."
msgstr ""

